### =====================================================================
### appointMe - day17-double-booking.http   (Day 17: the database says NO)
### SELF-CONTAINED: it logs in by itself and keeps its own tokens.
###
### BEFORE YOU START (and before every re-run of this file)
###   1. V4__no_overlapping_appointments.sql must be applied (start the app once).
###   2. Reload the seed:
###        Get-Content .\scripts\dev-seed.sql | docker exec -i appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme
###      (The seed restores Bob's normal week: Mon-Fri 09:00-13:00 and 14:00-18:00.)
###
### All bookings are on Tuesday 2027-02-02, Haircut = 30 minutes, customer 1.
### Times below are UTC (Z). Tenant 1 is Europe/Athens = UTC+2 in February,
### so 10:00Z is 12:00 on the clock in Athens.
###
### IMPORTANT: today a clash is NOT yet a clean 409. The API will answer with an ERROR status
### (probably 500) because nothing translates the database error yet. That is exactly what
### Day 18 fixes. What matters today: the clash is NEVER a 201, and nothing is stored.
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080


### ======================================================================
### SETUP
### ======================================================================

### O1. Alice logs in. EXPECT 200
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "alice@test.com", "password": "correct-horse-1" }

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceUserToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}

### O2. Alice selects tenant 1. EXPECT 200, OWNER
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/select-tenant/1
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceUserToken}}

> {%
    client.global.set("aliceToken", response.body.accessToken);
%}


### ======================================================================
### 1. THE CONSTRAINT THROUGH YOUR API
### ======================================================================

### C1. Book Bob 10:00Z-10:30Z. EXPECT 201 (remember its id)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z", "notes": "first" }

> {%
    client.global.set("firstApptId", response.body.id);
    client.test("C1: booked", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### C2. EXACTLY the same slot again. EXPECT an ERROR status (NOT 201).
###     Today probably 500; after Day 18 it will be 409.
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z", "notes": "duplicate" }

> {%
    client.test("C2: duplicate refused (not 201)", function () {
        client.assert(response.status !== 201, "the duplicate was ACCEPTED, status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### C3. Partial overlap, 10:15Z-10:45Z. EXPECT an ERROR status (NOT 201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:15:00Z", "notes": "overlap" }

> {%
    client.test("C3: overlap refused (not 201)", function () {
        client.assert(response.status !== 201, "the overlap was ACCEPTED, status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### C4. Back-to-back, 10:30Z-11:00Z. EXPECT 201 (the end of one is the start of the next)
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:30:00Z", "notes": "back to back" }

> {%
    client.test("C4: back-to-back allowed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}

### C5. A DIFFERENT staff member (Alice herself, membership 1) at the same time. EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 1, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z", "notes": "other staff" }

> {%
    client.test("C5: different staff allowed", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### 2. CANCELLING FREES THE SLOT
### ======================================================================

### C6. Cancel the first appointment. EXPECT 200, CANCELLED
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/appointments/{{firstApptId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "status": "CANCELLED" }

### C7. Book Bob 10:00Z again (the slot C1 had). EXPECT 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/appointments
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "staffId": 2, "customerId": 1, "serviceId": 1, "startsAt": "2027-02-02T10:00:00Z", "notes": "re-booked" }

> {%
    client.test("C7: slot reused after cancel", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201, "status " + response.status);
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### 3. AVAILABILITY (Day 16) AND THE CONSTRAINT AGREE
### Bob is now busy 10:00Z-11:00Z = 12:00-13:00 Athens time (C7 + C4).
### ======================================================================

### C8. Bob's free slots, Tuesday 2027-02-02, Haircut. EXPECT 200 and 26 slots
###     (30 without bookings). Morning slots 11:45, 12:00, 12:15 and 12:30 are gone;
###     11:30 and the afternoon 14:00 ... 17:30 are still there.
GET {{baseUrl}}/availability?staffId=2&serviceId=1&date=2027-02-02
Authorization: Bearer {{aliceToken}}

> {%
    client.test("C8: 26 slots, the booked hour is gone", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "status " + response.status);
        var starts = response.body.slots.map(function (x) { return x.startsAt; });
        client.assert(starts.length === 26, "slot count " + starts.length);
        client.assert(starts.indexOf("2027-02-02T11:30:00+02:00") >= 0, "11:30 should be free");
        client.assert(starts.indexOf("2027-02-02T11:45:00+02:00") < 0, "11:45 should be gone");
        client.assert(starts.indexOf("2027-02-02T12:30:00+02:00") < 0, "12:30 should be gone");
        client.assert(starts.indexOf("2027-02-02T14:00:00+02:00") >= 0, "14:00 should be free");
    });
%}


### ======================================================================
### 4. WHAT THE DATABASE SAW (run these in PowerShell, not here)
### ======================================================================
###   docker exec -it appointme-db psql -U appointme -d appointme -c "SELECT id, staff_id, starts_at, ends_at, status, notes FROM appointments WHERE starts_at::date = '2027-02-02' ORDER BY staff_id, starts_at;"
###
### EXPECT 4 rows: Bob "first" CANCELLED, Bob "back to back", Bob "re-booked", Alice "other staff".
### The rejected duplicate and overlap are NOT there: a failed insert stores nothing.
### Notice the ids have GAPS (a rejected insert still used up an id). Sequences never roll back.
